{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"Tries","title":"Tries","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"},{"text":" is a set of sequences and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary"},{"text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"text":", whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"text":"), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"code":"Character","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"text":", and a radix tree’s to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matches: a trie of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns with failure links. Its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the automaton as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sets of sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"],"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences"},{"title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"],"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences"},{"title":"Pattern matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"],"anchor":"Pattern-matching"},{"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"kind":"symbol","title":"RadixTreeDictionary","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Trees","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Trie","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"TrieDictionary","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RadixTree"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"title":"Tries","url":"\/documentation\/tries","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofEdgeAt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"statesView"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":">."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV","text":"StatesView"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each state but the root to its failure state. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"text":" tells the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apart.","type":"text"}],"title":"statesView","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","type":"topic"}}}